{"id": "394a3efc-5490-43c8-b564-9671d5f94de3", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll run a lifecycle-policy audit across every ECR repository in this account/region, checking whether any image set for deletion is still in active use.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_95lO0ah4NtofFVPGXo99zb", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"deep_research": true, "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run the ecr-lifecycle-guard skill's full procedure across EVERY ECR repository in account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. For each repository: read its lifecycle policy (or note none attached), determine the expiring image set (prefer StartLifecyclePolicyPreview/GetLifecyclePolicyPreview — AUTHORITATIVE; fall back to SIMULATED only if preview cannot complete), cross-reference every expiring image against in-use evidence (lastRecordedPullTime tier (a); ECS running tasks/services/ACTIVE task definitions, Batch ACTIVE job definitions, Lambda container image functions, App Runner services tier (b); CloudTrail BatchGetImage/GetDownloadUrlForLayer with push-correlation filtering tier (c)), assign verdicts (Expiring-InUse / Expiring-Unknown / Expiring-Unused / Safe), and compute each repository's rating (Healthy/Attention/AtRisk/Indeterminate) per the skill's verdict model and 15-point check matrix.",
  "context": "User asked: 'Across every ECR repository in this account in us-east-1, will any lifecycle policy delete an image we are still running? Summarize by repository.' You MUST call skill_read on the 'ecr-lifecycle-guard' skill first and follow its Output Contract EXACTLY — the final report format with all required ## headings (Scope, Repository Rating, Source of Truth, Expiring Images, Rule by Rule, Findings, Suggested Protective Rule, Check Matrix, Not Assessed, Next Steps), literal verdict/rating vocabulary, and the Account Summary section for the multi-repository case (ordered AtRisk, Indeterminate, Attention, Healthy; full sections for every repo that is not Healthy). This is a read-only control-plane audit — never call any ECR/ECS/Batch/Lambda/AppRunner write action. StartLifecyclePolicyPreview may trigger an approval prompt; approve it once if asked, it changes nothing.",
  "resources": ["account: 012345678901_1", "region: us-east-1", "scope: all repositories returned by ecr DescribeRepositories in this account/region"],
  "timeframe": "pull recency window: default 30 days (per skill default)",
  "criteria": "Follow the skill's Execution Flow steps 1-9 verbatim, including the Catch All Count rule for tagStatus:any + imageCountMoreThan rules, the push-correlation rule for CloudTrail tier (c) evidence, and the full 15-row Check Matrix per repository. Return the complete rendered report produced by the skill verbatim — do not summarize or shorten it, since the parent will relay it unchanged to the user."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit ECR lifecycle policies across all repos in us-east-1 for in-use images"}], "created_at": null}
